  "prefLabel": "Env-A 4102.03 Aerosol adhesive",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 4102.03 “Aerosol adhesive” means an aerosol product in which the spray mechanism is permanently housed in a non-refillable can designed for hand-held application without the need for ancillary hoses or spray equipment. The term includes special purpose spray adhesives and web spray adhesives.\n\nSource. #10527, eff 2-26-14; ss by #13969, eff 5-21-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a4100.html"
